Here is the root cause:
The original implementation used a `SortedSet` to store authorizations, which may not have correctly handled the sorting of authorizations in a case-insensitive manner due to the way it was constructed and utilized. This could lead to unexpected ordering of the displayed authorizations, causing confusion or incorrect results when users queried their authorizations. The refactoring to a `List` and explicit sorting addresses this issue directly by ensuring that the authorizations are sorted correctly before being displayed.

